      "post": {
        "description": "Give one other Primer user read access.\n\nNothing is copied. The grantee reads the same library, the same\ndocuments and the same vectors the owner does - which is the whole point\nof sharing rather than duplicating, and why revoking is immediate: there\nis no second copy to go and find.\n\nOnly someone who has used this deployment can be named. User rows are\nwritten when an identity first acts, so an address that matches nothing\nbelongs either to a colleague who has not signed in yet or to a typo,\nand the two are worth telling apart out loud. That does disclose whether\nan address has an account here, to an authenticated user of the same\ndeployment - which is the trade for the feature being usable at all, and\nis a much smaller disclosure than sharing with the wrong person.",
        "operationId": "share_library_api_v1_libraries__library_id__shares_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "library_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Library Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
